Very well, it's confession time.  Here's a nethack abuse I tried once.
Once I decided (just to try something out) to restart nethack until I got a 
particular character (probably a wizard with a magic marker and a good 
ring or something). So I was starting and quitting, starting and quitting,
and then I decided to start a few nethacks at once, each in their own
window.

I guess even on this HP (UNIX), the random number generator is seeded by the
clock, because two of the nethacks I started right after each other were 
exactly the same: Same inventory, same level 1, same potions assigned to 
each color.  I tried playing one game just to test things out, and then
using what I learned in the other game.  In the test game, I got into 
trouble, so I entered discovery mode, and continued to identify everything.

This was a kind of neat way to identify things, but way too time consuming
-- if I wanted to cheat, I could do it a lot easier than that.  As for the
game, some stupid death (lost in the annals of history) claimed the 
character.
